# Desktop client build-time configuration (dev-release, design §C / Data Models).
#
# Copy to `.env` (or `.env.dev`) and fill in before building the dev installer:
#   electron-vite build        # bakes MAIN_VITE_* into out/main
#   npm run build:win          # produces the NSIS .exe with these values baked in
#
# How it works: electron-vite loads these vars and inlines any prefixed with
# MAIN_VITE_ into the MAIN process bundle as `import.meta.env.MAIN_VITE_*`.
# They are therefore BAKED AT BUILD TIME into the packaged .exe.
#
# IMPORTANT — these are PUBLIC values, NOT secrets (Req 2.5):
#   * the Supabase ANON (publishable) key is designed to ship in clients
#   * the backend / gateway / Supabase URLs are public endpoints
# No Provider_Secret (Deepgram, Groq/Gemini, Supabase service-role key) EVER
# belongs in the desktop client or in this file. Those live only on the host.
#
# Do NOT commit a real `.env` (it is gitignored). Commit only this example.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Resolved environment for the packaged build. `dev` makes the client target
# the hosted dev backend and require sign-in (enforced auth).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
MAIN_VITE_APP_ENV=dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# dev environment endpoints + Supabase publishable key (public, baked in).
# Replace the placeholders with your hosted dev values:
#   <app> = your Railway service subdomain (stable *.up.railway.app)
#   <ref> = your Supabase project ref
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
MAIN_VITE_DEV_BACKEND_URL=https://<app>.up.railway.app
MAIN_VITE_DEV_GATEWAY_URL=wss://<app>.up.railway.app
MAIN_VITE_DEV_SUPABASE_URL=https://<ref>.supabase.co
MAIN_VITE_DEV_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<publishable-anon-key>
